## ef508bd1 Get and renew the link's certificate on its own, and switch the tunnel to https when the relay passes it through

LinkTls orders through the tunnel, renews inside the window the CA suggests, backs off as Let's Encrypt's limits ask, and moves the tunnel to https only with the certificate in the listener, more than a day left, and a relay that says it passes TLS through, and then only if a probe through the link finds that very certificate. GET /api/link now tells the link's encryption, with the four fields of TlsView. A machine that only reads orders nothing: main.ts runs the manager's timers under ctx.mode.whenLead.

Proved by link-tls.test.ts, tls-checks.test.ts, link.test.ts and setup.test.ts. npm run test:real was not run, since this build uses no Docker; this change does not touch what it tests.

Ruling: main.ts starts the manager through ctx.mode.whenLead, not a bare ctx.tls.start() - why: the lead's note and plan 2's own wording, a machine that reads must not order or renew - cost if wrong: one line in main.ts.
Ruling: tick() after stop() does nothing, and a pass that a stop overtakes moves no mode and writes no tunnel, though an order under way ends - why: a stale pass on a machine that stopped leading could rewrite tunnel.json - cost if wrong: one order finishes on a machine leaving lead mode, and the next leader's first pass probes.
Ruling: no listener given counts as not holding the certificate, so http - why: fail toward a working link, and plan 2 says link-tls.test.ts gives LinkTls a fake Served - cost if wrong: a LinkTls with no serveOn never leaves http.
Ruling: while the relay says up and passthrough and the block runs, the wanted mode is http - why: the plan's sentence leaves this case open, and a row under a block is in http anyway - cost if wrong: none seen.
Ruling: PublicLinks.sync() goes in turn with set and remove, which write through a private writeSettings - why: the manager is a second writer of tunnel.json, and a write that read the link before a rename could land after the rename's own and keep the old link - cost if wrong: a sync waits up to the relay's timeouts of a change under way.
Ruling: TlsView.mode comes from linkMode, not the row - why: right after a rename the row still says https while tunnel.json says http, and the view should say what the tunnel does - cost if wrong: two more reads per GET /api/link.
Ruling: anything but an AcmeError in the order's path counts as invalid - why: one wait and one log line with kind and type only, so a failure's text never reaches the log - cost if wrong: a programming error reads as invalid in the row.
Ruling: SAN names compare lowercased through namesHost in x509.ts, used by the manager and store.ts's mayRunHttps; LEAST_LEFT_MS is exported from store.ts - why: the lead's carry from Task 7 and one decision in one place, though both files lie outside the task's list - cost if wrong: none seen.
Ruling: accountDoesNotExist drops accountUrl and orders once more, keeping replaces - why: the plan and the lead's carry; each refusal gives up one of the two, so an order comes back at most twice - cost if wrong: one extra order on a CA that refuses both.

